comments:
@jason-bragg what other means for removing duplicates would you suggest?

I doubt we'll see any other implementation of `IApplicationPart` any time soon (or maybe ever) and if we do, they design is up to the implementer. The only sensible use for a custom implementation would be if it were paired with a custom `IApplicationFeatureProvider` and the semantics for that are totally up to them in that case.

In the worst case, with no deduplication, the end-consumers of these parts tend to deduplicate anyway, since the parts feed Dictionaries keyed on CLR types (string, Type, int)

@ReubenBond, I'm cool with that.

I very slightly favor the feature provider being responsible for deduping parts, as it would have a better understanding of the parts and if duplicates should be allowed, but this is an extremely minor preference.

Inheriting from IEquatable seems to me a viable solution.
